revision 56848
shortdesc Hungarian dummy text (Lorum ipse)
longdesc Lorem ipsum is an improper Latin filler dummy text, cf. the
longdesc lipsum package. It is commonly used for demonstrating the
longdesc textual elements of a document template. Lorum ipse is a
longdesc Hungarian variation of Lorem ipsum. (Lorum is a Hungarian card
longdesc game, and ipse is a Hungarian slang word meaning bloke.) With
longdesc this package you can typeset 150 paragraphs of Lorum ipse. All
longdesc paragraphs are taken with permission from
longdesc http://www.lorumipse.hu. Thanks to Lorum Ipse Lab (Viktor Nagy
longdesc and David Takacs) for their work.
